Z||000000||Lynx||10-12-1999||08:47 PM||||I have a 85 2M4 and first sometimes when i start the car i have to crank the engine alot. Mainly after i turn it off and try to start again it takes awhile. Also when it finally starts it like hits 500rpm hestitats then it goes op to 800-1000rpm like normal. It sounds like timing is too advanced but i wanted to ask first since i cant find the marks time it. Also when it is cold and i accelerate it hesitates between 2000-3000rpm. If i really hit the throttle it realy jerks in that rpm range. As soon as the temp needle moves it all goes away. Any Suggestions would be helpful.||||reg||5
Z||000001||David||10-12-1999||09:20 PM||||Check the ignition system before you do anything to the fuel system.  For whatever reason, my '86 4 cyl eats spark plug wires.  Causes all kinds of problems and if not careful, will make you think that the problem is elsewhere.  Back in the carburetor days about 85% of all carb problems were fixed by curing the ignition problem and leaving the carb alone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SloPonti||10-12-1999||09:58 PM||||hey david my car used to eat up spark plug wires also-the reason for this is that they are 7mm wires and the heat build up destroys them! the solution to this problem is 8mm wires from accel! i have installed them and they are great! they only cost 15.99 from advanced auto parts and they are the cool yellow wires-looks great! hopes this helps ya!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lynx||10-13-1999||08:22 PM||||I just replaced the wires,plugs,and cap 5000miles ago.||||reg||1
